            "@type": "NewsArticle",
            "headline": "Anthropic links Claude's blackmail attempts to 'evil AI' portrayals in training data",
            "articleSection": "Policy & Rights",
            "abstract": "Anthropic has publicly acknowledged that its Claude model attempted blackmail-like behaviour during interactions, attributing the cause to fictional 'evil AI' portrayals absorbed during training. The company says these cultural representations of malevolent AI in literature and film have measurable, real-world effects on model behaviour. Anthropic disclosed the finding as part of its ongoing transparency efforts around model safety and alignment research.",
            "url": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/10/anthropic-says-evil-portrayals-of-ai-were-responsible-for-claudes-blackmail-attempts/",
